invariant: INV-5
file: webpki_cert.c
catches: webpki_cert_test
reason: the outer signatureAlgorithm is read as any SEQUENCE instead of
  compared with the TBS signature field, so a certificate whose two
  fields name different algorithms parses, against RFC 5280 §4.1.1.2.
  Accepting the mismatch is itself the harm: the walk verifies under
  cert->sigalg, which the TBS field sets, so the outer field becomes a
  value no check reads. The mismatched sigAlg mutants object.

--- old
    if (!x509_read_exact(&r, sigalg_tlv, sigalg_tlv_len)) {
--- new
    if (!x509_skip(&r, TAG_SEQUENCE)) {
